Let me elaborate on this.  Assuming I'm a potential corporate sponsor,
here are some of the questions I'd need answers to before I would
consider any kind of investment:

1). What is the total established user base for Nethack?
2). What are the demographics of this user base?
3). How much in dollars/technical resources is it going to cost
me to reach this user base?
4). How will my participation in this be perceived by the market
as a whole?
5). Are there long-term requirements for continued support?
6). Most important: who am I going to make this deal with?  I'm
not just going to release my own version of Nethack, because it's
not going to be widely adopted any more than any of the other patches
to Nethack are widely adopted.  Presumably, I'd need a deal with the
Dev Team, but are they even an "entity" in the sense that they can
enter into a long-term, legally binding contract?  I need contractual
guarantees that my branding is going to make it into the widely
adopted version of the game, is there an entity that can be held
to account if this doesn't happen?
7). Also important: is there a guarantee on _when_ my branding will
make it into the widely adopted version of the game?  I would want
a hard-and-fast schedule so that I could time the release with other
PR/media to make the most of my contribution.  "Whenever we get around
to releasing NH 3.5.1" doesn't cut it.

Those are just off the top of my head...  The real concern for anyone
in a marketing postition will be, "if I take this proposal to my boss,
is it going to get me fired?"  Without good answers for the above
questions, anyone making this proposal _should_ be fired.


